SUMMARY:Deadline 13:00 CET: Casa de Velazquez: Artists in Residence 2027-20
 28 (Academie de France a Madrid)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 27 Nov 2026 at 13:00 CET.\n\nThe Academie de France a Ma
 drid at the Casa de Velazquez offers 12 one-year residencies for 2027-2028
  to young graduates and established artists developing a creative project 
 in the Iberian Peninsula.\n\nOrganisation: Casa de Velazquez\, Academie de
  France a Madrid\nLocation: Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velaz
 quez). No nationality requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affi
 liated to an artist/author or self-employed scheme in their country of res
 idence\, and non-EU applicants need a French residence permit allowing wor
 k or a Schengen work and residence permit from another EU state. Good Fren
 ch required.\nAward: Monthly residency grant voted each year\; for 2026-20
 27 it was EUR 3\,600 per month for artists housed at the Casa and EUR 4\,6
 00 per month for artists living outside (with children). Twelve monthly pa
 yments\, September 2027 to August 2028. Housing and studio provided\; a pr
 oduction support fund is also available on project. No application fee.\nD
 uration: 12 months (1 September 2027 to 31 August 2028\; on site mid-Septe
 mber to about 20 July)\n\nMore: https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-e
 n-la-casa/detail/appel-artistes-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-en-la-casa/detail/appel-artist
 es-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velazquez). No nationalit
 y requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affiliated to an artist/
 author or self-employed scheme in their country of residence\, and non-EU 
 applicants need a French residence permit allowing work or a Schengen work
  and residence permit from another EU state. Good French required.
END:VEVENT
