SUMMARY:Deadline: Internationale Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen: Call for Films\, 
 73rd Festival (2027)
DESCRIPTION:The 73rd International Short Film Festival Oberhausen (27 April
  to 2 May 2027)\, one of the oldest and most influential short film festiv
 als\, opens its call for films across five competitions: International (ma
 x 35 minutes\, produced outside Germany\, German festival premiere require
 d)\, German (max 45 minutes\, produced in Germany\, no premiere requiremen
 t)\, NRW (max 45 minutes\, produced or...\n\nOrganisation: Internationale 
 Kurzfilmtage Oberhausen (International Short Film Festival Oberhausen)\nLo
 cation: Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.\nAward: International Competiti
 on: Grand Prize of the City of Oberhausen EUR 8\,000\, Principal Prize EUR
  4\,000\, Promotional Prize EUR 1\,500\, plus a European Film Awards short
  film nomination. German Competition: EUR 5\,000 main prize\, EUR 1\,500 p
 romotional\, EUR 2\,500 3sat Emerging Talent Prize (with purchase offer)\,
  EUR 1\,000 ZONTA Prize for a female filmmaker. NRW Competition: EUR 1\,00
 0 and EUR 500 prizes\, plus NRW Ministry prizes of EUR 5\,000 and EUR 3\,0
 00\, FIPRESCI Prize\, EUR 2\,000 Ecumenical Jury Prize\, EUR 750 WDR Westa
 rt Audience Jury Prize. Children's and Youth: several EUR 1\,000-1\,500 pr
 izes and an ECFA Short Film Award nomination. Prizes go to the directors. 
 SUBMISSION FEE: first five submissions per submitter are free\; EUR 20 han
 dling fee per film from the sixth.\nDuration: Festival runs 27 April to 2 
 May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kurzfilmtage.de/en/festival/submission/?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Oberhausen\, Germany. International Competition open to production
 s from outside Germany (plus co-productions)\; separate German\, NRW\, Chi
 ldren's and Youth\, and MuVi competitions.
END:VEVENT
