SUMMARY:Deadline: HIAP: Ukraine Solidarity Residencies Programme 2027 (Finl
 and)
DESCRIPTION:The Ukraine Solidarity Residencies Programme (USRP)\, run by HI
 AP with partner residencies and supported by the Finnish Ministry of Educa
 tion and Culture\, offers residencies across Finland for professional Ukra
 inian or Ukraine-based artists and arts practitioners affected by the war\
 , whether still in Ukraine or based elsewhere.\n\nOrganisation: HIAP (Hels
 inki International Artist Programme) and partner residencies\nLocation: Se
 ven residencies across Finland: HIAP Suomenlinna (Helsinki)\, AARK (Korpo\
 , Turku Archipelago)\, Art Centre Salmela (Mantyharju)\, Fairres (Porvoo)\
 , Nelimarkka Artist Residency (Alajarvi)\, Vartsila Art House (North Karel
 ia) and Gjutars Artists House (Vantaa). Open to Ukrainian or Ukraine-based
  artists.\nAward: Working grant of EUR 1\,200 per month (EUR 1\,200 to 3\,
 600 depending on residency length)\, plus free living and working space\, 
 one return trip from the artist's home\, and a small access budget for dis
 abled artists. No application fee.\nDuration: 1 to 3 months (extension pos
 sible)\, between January and July 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiap.fi/open-
 call/open-call-for-ukrainian-and-ukraine-based-artists-in-finland-2027/?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
